# Byte-for-byte checkouts on every platform. Do not remove.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config, so a fresh clone or any
# `git checkout` / `git stash` / `git reset --hard` would rewrite every text file to CRLF.
# That breaks three things this project depends on:
#
#   1. version/MANIFEST.sha256 -- the integrity check every session starts with. Changing
#      the line endings changes every text file's hash, so the check would report ~100
#      failures that are not real changes.
#   2. version/CODE_SNAPSHOT.txt -- same problem, split back and compared.
#   3. tools/**/*.sh -- a shell script with CRLF fails in WSL and in the sandbox with
#      "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M", which reads as a broken script rather than a broken
#      checkout.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion entirely: what was committed is what lands on
# disk, on Windows and Linux alike. This repo round-trips between the two, so that is the
# only setting under which the hashes mean anything.
* -text
